      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 3,
            "text": "Multiple Choice Questions"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "1. A hypothesis is:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) A final result",
              "(b) A test value",
              "(c) A proposed explanation",
              "(d) A dataset"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "2. The null hypothesis represents:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) An alternative idea",
              "(b) No effect or no difference",
              "(c) A final conclusion",
              "(d) A prediction model"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "3. The symbol used for the null hypothesis is:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) (H_1)",
              "(b) (H_2)",
              "(c) (H_0)",
              "(d) (H_x)"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "4. A p-value is used for:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) Measuring accuracy",
              "(b) Testing a hypothesis",
              "(c) Measuring variance",
              "(d) Data storage"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "5. If (p-value < α ), the decision is to:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) Accept (H_0)",
              "(b) Reject (H_0)",
              "(c) Ignore data",
              "(d) Recalculate the mean"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "6. The critical region is the:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) Safe area",
              "(b) Rejection area",
              "(c) Data range",
              "(d) Sample space"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "7. An example of a test statistic is:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) Mean",
              "(b) t-value",
              "(c) Mode",
              "(d) Median"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "8. Data visualisation is used to:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) Store data",
              "(b) Present results clearly",
              "(c) Delete data",
              "(d) Calculate the mean"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "9. A chart useful for comparison is:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) Pie chart",
              "(b) Bar chart",
              "(c) Table",
              "(d) Text"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "10. Bias in data means:"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "(a) Correct data",
              "(b) Balanced data",
              "(c) Unfair representation",
              "(d) Random data"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 3,
            "text": "Short Questions"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": true,
            "items": [
              "What is a hypothesis?",
              "What is a research question?",
              "Define null hypothesis (H₀).",
              "What is a test statistic?",
              "What is meant by p-value?",
              "What is a critical region?",
              "What are the basic steps in hypothesis testing?",
              "Why is data visualization important?",
              "What is bias in data collection?",
              "Why is ethical use of data important?"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 3,
            "text": "Long Questions"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": true,
            "items": [
              "Explain the concept of hypothesis testing and its role in data analysis.",
              "Describe different types of hypotheses and explain how to formulate correct hypotheses.",
              "Explain key concepts in hypothesis testing, including test statistics, critical region, and p-value.",
              "Discuss the steps involved in performing hypothesis testing with a suitable example.",
              "Explain the importance of data visualization in hypothesis testing and how graphs help present results.",
              "Discuss ethical issues in data science, including bias, ethical use of data, and responsible communication.",
              "Explain how to interpret hypothesis testing results and connect conclusions to hypotheses.",
              "Describe how findings should be communicated clearly in data analysis and why it is important."
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
